{
  "requirement": "The harness MUST expose:\n\n```text\nfinish_search({ search_id: UUID, used: Array<String> })\n    -> { search_id: UUID, finished: true }\n```\n\nThe arguments MUST contain exactly these fields.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.authoring.finish_search`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. The harness exposes `finish_search({search_id: UUID, used: Array<String>})`.\n2. The arguments contain exactly the fields `search_id` and `used`.\n3. The result is `{search_id, finished: true}`.\n\n**Obligation 1: exposure and signature**\n- `src/authoring/tools.rs#mod[tests]/fn[finish_search_advertises_the_accounting_schema_and_selection_rule]` asserts the full parameter schema. It requires `search_id` as a uuid-format string, `used` as an array of strings, `required: [search_id, used]`, and `additionalProperties: false`. It also checks the description.\n- `src/authoring/tools.rs#fn[dispatch_paged]` routes the `finish_search` name to `pages.finish_search`.\n- In `src/authoring/mod.rs`, the test `SearchProvider` calls the tool by name `finish_search` with `{search_id, used}`. The integration tests that use it assert `tool_calls[\"finish_search\"]` counts, so the tool is reachable end to end.\n- `src/authoring/searches.rs#mod[tests]/fn[delivered_searches_including_empty_results_need_explicit_completion]` calls `finish_search` in the same way for empty and repeated searches.\n\n**Obligation 2: exactly these fields**\n- `src/authoring/searches.rs#mod[tests]/fn[invalid_completion_is_atomic_and_can_be_corrected]` feeds each of these malformed argument sets into `finish_search` and asserts the error message:\n  - null, an array, and `{}`\n  - a missing `used`\n  - a missing `search_id`\n  - an extra field\n  - a non-string `search_id` and a malformed UUID string\n  - an unknown but well-formed UUID\n  - a `used` value that is null, a string, or an array with a non-string element\n- Each of these is rejected with \"exactly search_id and used\" or the matching type error.\n- The test also checks that a rejected call leaves the search outstanding and records no inputs, and that a corrected call then succeeds.\n- Together with the schema's `additionalProperties:false` and `required`, this covers \"exactly these fields\" for missing, extra, and mistyped arguments.\n\n**Obligation 3: result shape**\n- `selected_dependencies_keep_the_delivered_hash_and_accumulate_without_reads` asserts that `finish.result` equals `json!({\"search_id\":..., \"finished\":true})` exactly. It also asserts there is no `text` field.\n- `delivered_searches_including_empty_results_need_explicit_completion` asserts the same exact equality for each of three searches, including an empty result.\n\n**Gaps**\nNone found. Each obligation has an exercising test with a concrete assertion, and the tests carry `{test}` references to the subject. Sub-behaviours such as completion, deduplication and atomicity belong to the refining `finish_search.*` requirements, which are assessed separately.",
  "references": "fb30bb4d08c7c2e4bc72f39568c837260ff783f460dbaac22396bf020e8d6484",
